I agree here, too.  However, for me only those conducts are worth 
playing that can be done with *any* character, i.e., that don't need 
rerolling.  You see, for a decent player it is possible without much 
difficulty to get an ascension rate of 95% or better, if you allow 
rerolling, or just don't continue to play those characters that seem to 
have too weak stats or too poor equipment.  For me, the challenge is to 
play any character that I get as well as possible, and to make all of 
them survive.  Once I create a character, I am responsible for it... 
He/she is not material to just be thrown away, if he/she does not have a 
blindfold and I want to play blindly or a ring of slow digestion and I 
want to go without food...  And it would be irresponsible to let a 
character die that could survive by a wish or the breaking of some other 
conduct...  I have played the "easy" conducts, i.e. wishless, genoless 
and polypileless (all together), but only because I saw the character (a 
knight) could make it, having found an early cloak of MR.

